  <!-- ==================== ABOUT ==================== -->
  <section id="about" style="background: var(--sand-100);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="img-placeholder light reveal">
          <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M3 21h18"/><path d="M5 21V9l7-5 7 5v12"/><path d="M9 21v-6h6v6"/></svg>
          <span class="ph-label">Photo needed</span>
          <span class="ph-sub">Oceanus workshop at North Saanich Marina</span>
        </div>
        <div class="about-copy reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">About Us</span>
          <h2>Composites manufacturing, done to spec</h2>
          <p class="lead">Oceanus Reinforced Plastics specializes in semi-custom composites manufacturing, via hand layup and/or vacuum infusion.</p>
          <p>Working out of North Saanich Marina puts us in daily contact with boat owners, builders and marine trades who need composite parts made right — whether that's a single repair or a run of matching components.</p>
          <p>We keep both manufacturing methods in-house so the process fits the part, not the other way around.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid cols-3 mt-lg">
        <div class="card service-card reveal">
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="icon-badge"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 3"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Right method for the part</h3>
            <p>We recommend hand layup or vacuum infusion based on your part's shape, strength needs and volume.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card service-card reveal">
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="icon-badge"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M12 20c4-4 8-7.5 8-12a8 8 0 1 0-16 0c0 4.5 4 8 8 12Z"/><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="2.5"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Direct communication</h3>
            <p>You work directly with the people manufacturing your part, from quote to delivery.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card service-card reveal">
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="icon-badge"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></div>
            <h3>Built to spec</h3>
            <p>Every part is semi-custom — manufactured against your requirements, not a fixed catalogue.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== FAQ ==================== -->
  <section id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list reveal">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-1">
            What's the difference between hand layup and vacuum infusion?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-1">
            <p>Hand layup places resin and fibreglass by hand, which suits custom shapes and repairs. Vacuum infusion draws resin through the fibre under vacuum, giving a lighter, more consistent part — better suited to structural or higher-precision components. We'll recommend the right method for your project.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">
            What size or type of projects do you take on?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-2">
            <p>We manufacture semi-custom parts for marine and industrial applications, from individual components and repairs to short production runs. Contact us with your project details and we'll confirm whether it's a fit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">
            Do you build one-off parts, or only production runs?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-3">
            <p>Both. Our semi-custom approach covers single custom parts as well as short production runs using shared tooling.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">
            Where are you located, and do you serve clients outside North Saanich?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-4">
            <p>We're based at North Saanich Marina, 1949 Marina Way, North Saanich, BC. We work with clients across British Columbia — contact us to confirm delivery or pickup arrangements for your area.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">
            Do I need my own mold or design, or can you help develop one?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-5">
            <p>Either. If you have an existing mold or pattern we can work from it, and we also build custom molds and tooling for new parts. Share your project details and we'll advise on the best approach.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-6">
            How do I get a quote?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-6">
            <p>Fill out the contact form or call us at (250) 656-7733 with your project details. We'll follow up to discuss scope, materials and timeline before confirming a price.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-7">
            What are your hours, and how do I reach you?
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-7">
            <p>We're open weekdays from 8:00 a.m. and closed on weekends. Call (250) 656-7733 to confirm same-day hours, or reach us anytime through the contact form.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

